-- The error limit. One mistake in a layout-sensitive language routinely costs a diagnostic per
-- production that gave up on it, so a file broken enough to pass the limit is one where the next
-- message says nothing the first fifty did not - and a server that reparses on every keystroke
-- pays for each of them. The fifty-first message is the one that says the rest are missing.
--
-- Recovery itself does not stop: the declarations below the flood are all still in the AST, which
-- is the half of a parse an editor reads even when it shows no diagnostics at all.

fn before() -> Int = 1

